Sources
-------

- Z-Anatomy, https://www.z-anatomy.com/ (CC BY-SA 4.0): the named, grouped
  and reworked meshes of the skeleton, muscles and joints, and the Latin
  terms.
- BodyParts3D, The Database Center for Life Science,
  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/ (CC BY 4.0 since
  2025-02-27; earlier releases CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan): the anatomical geometry
  Z-Anatomy is built on.
- Taken from the browser export of Z-Anatomy in
  https://github.com/nqwrc/3d-anatomy at commit
  8ca3b7421bcfbe88b85859eb1983d5cf79f21749: public/models/skeletal.glb,
  muscular.glb, joints.glb and public/data/lexicon.json.

Not included: the non-commercial parts of Z-Anatomy (the inner ear,
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and the kidney, CC BY-NC 4.0), nor organs, vessels or
nerves.

Changes
-------

The meshes were decoded from Draco compression and stored with positions
quantised to 16 bits within each mesh's bounds; normals were left out and
are recomputed by the app. Nothing was simplified, moved or reshaped. The
tool that does this is tools/atlas/build_human_pack.py.
